WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.515
Dedicated browser profiles separate research history, bookmarks, cookies, settings,

00:00:04.515 --> 00:00:06.060
and accounts from personal browsing.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.660
Profiles can also separate cases when policy requires stronger boundaries,

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.440
but too many profiles become difficult to patch and manage.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:16.320
Build a small bookmark structure around workflow: approved search services,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.465
official records, technical references, archive services, internal policy,

00:00:20.465 --> 00:00:21.970
and reporting resources.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.610
Review bookmarks periodically because services change, disappear, or alter their terms.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.485
Extensions should be installed carefully.

00:00:28.485 --> 00:00:31.080
Every extension adds permissions, update dependencies,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.210
and potential access to browsing data.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.110
Prefer a minimal approved set, verify the publisher and required permissions,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.925
and remove tools that no longer provide clear workflow value.

00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:43.080
Screenshot and archive tools should preserve source context,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.811
not create isolated fragments.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.794
Record the URL, title, timestamp, and reason for capture.

00:00:47.794 --> 00:00:50.280
A screenshot is a representation of what was visible,

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.300
while an archive may have coverage gaps or preservation limits.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.459
Keep personal email, social, cloud, and shopping accounts out of the research profile.

00:00:57.459 --> 00:01:01.180
Account separation reduces accidental posting, unwanted personalization,

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.660
and leakage between personal and case activity.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.110
It does not authorize false identities or access to private areas.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.440
Standardize the environment with documented settings, update checks,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.510
and a known export path into the case structure.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.410
The browser should make collection more consistent while preserving human judgment about

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.305
source reliability,

00:01:18.305 --> 00:01:18.960
privacy, and scope.
